1
00:00:00,261 --> 00:00:01,817
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝

2
00:00:02,373 --> 00:00:03,400
بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

3
00:00:05,278 --> 00:00:08,868
اَلْحَمْدُ لله وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

4
00:00:10,796 --> 00:00:11,629
Chapter 6:

5
00:00:14,844 --> 00:00:17,635
The virtue of injury in the sake of Allah.

6
00:00:18,722 --> 00:00:23,008
Abu Hurairah(أبوهريرة) narrated Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

7
00:00:23,579 --> 00:00:25,635
Anyone who is injured in the path of Allah,

8
00:00:26,270 --> 00:00:28,059
And Allah knows who is injured in His sake,

9
00:00:28,424 --> 00:00:30,917
He will come on the Day of Judgment with his injury bleeding.

10
00:00:31,472 --> 00:00:34,456
The color is that of blood, and the smell is that of musk,

11
00:00:34,948 --> 00:00:35,797
Bukhari(بخاريْ) and Muslim(ألمسلم).

12
00:00:36,861 --> 00:00:41,507
Ibn Daqiq Al Eid(إبن دقيق ألعيد), he says the presentation of injury on the Day of Judgment indicates two things.

13
00:00:43,008 --> 00:00:45,278
Number one injury is the witness for the person.

14
00:00:45,754 --> 00:00:49,323
Number two, it's a badge of honor for the person in front of all creation.

15
00:00:49,657 --> 00:00:50,419
Ayesha(عائشه) said:

16
00:00:51,459 --> 00:00:55,697
Whenever Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, would remember the day of Uhud(أحَد), he would say

17
00:00:56,078 --> 00:00:57,859
that is a day that belongs to Talha(طلحة).

18
00:00:59,303 --> 00:01:01,510
I was the first to go back to the Messenger of Allah,

19
00:01:02,184 --> 00:01:06,443
but I found a man fighting with him and I said to myself, be Talha(طلحة) until he said,

20
00:01:06,999 --> 00:01:11,570
Talha(طلحة) had run 70 injuries in his body and his hand was cut off.

21
00:01:11,911 --> 00:01:13,078
Urwah Bin Zubair(عُروة بن زبير) said:

22
00:01:13,348 --> 00:01:16,181
Zubair(زبير) had three scars from sword wounds.

23
00:01:17,030 --> 00:01:21,990
One was on his shoulder, it was so large, I would stick my fingers in it.

24
00:01:23,101 --> 00:01:26,048
Two of them were from Badr(بدر), and one in the Battle of Yarmook(يرموك).

25
00:01:26,175 --> 00:01:32,390
Urwah(عُروة) is, his son, who used to play with injuries of his father, the scars.

26
00:01:34,136 --> 00:01:35,192
Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك) said:

27
00:01:36,263 --> 00:01:40,797
Abu Dughanna(أبودغنة) throw himself behind the walls in Yamamah(يمامة) and his leg broke.

28
00:01:41,388 --> 00:01:44,476
He kept on fighting with a broken leg, until he was killed,

29
00:01:44,936 --> 00:01:45,686
Alam Al-Nabola(أعلام ألنبلاء).

30
00:01:47,368 --> 00:01:49,900
Ma'az Ibn Amr Bin Jamooh(معاذ إبن عمرو بن جموح), he said:

31
00:01:49,932 --> 00:01:52,203
I made the Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) my Target on the day of Badr(بدر),

32
00:01:53,226 --> 00:01:57,123
when I found him I charged at him and hit him with my sword and cut his leg in two,

33
00:01:58,393 --> 00:02:03,416
then his son Ikrama(عكرمة) hit me on my shoulder, until he cut my arm off.

34
00:02:05,527 --> 00:02:08,959
It's only remained hanging through my body by the skin of my side.

35
00:02:09,567 --> 00:02:14,576
So the arm is cut is only hanging on the skin of the side.

36
00:02:18,156 --> 00:02:23,060
But because fighting distracted me, I remain dragging it behind me for most of the day,

37
00:02:23,314 --> 00:02:24,362
he didn't even take a break.

38
00:02:25,441 --> 00:02:30,987
Dragging my arm behind me annoyed me, so I placed my foot over it and pulled it off.

39
00:02:33,067 --> 00:02:35,065
During the Battle of Yamamah(يمامة), you know,

40
00:02:35,462 --> 00:02:43,190
contrast that with, when there's a small knife cut on your finger and you put bandage on it and it's emergency at home,

41
00:02:43,944 --> 00:02:49,672
during the Battle of Yamamah(يمامة), the first one to leave the Battleground was a Abu Aqeel(أبوعقيل), one of the Ansaar(أنصار).

42
00:02:50,503 --> 00:02:53,975
An Arrow that hit him between his shoulder and his heart injured him.

43
00:02:54,670 --> 00:02:56,090
He was then carried to the camp.

44
00:02:57,113 --> 00:02:59,511
When the battle was turning against the Muslims, he heard,

45
00:02:59,987 --> 00:03:02,984
Ma'an Ibn Odae(معن إبن عدئ) calling the Ansaar(أنصار) to charge the enemy.

46
00:03:03,857 --> 00:03:07,181
Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عمر) said: Abu Aqeel(أبوعقيل) stood up, so I asked him, What do you want to do?

47
00:03:07,865 --> 00:03:09,508
He replied: They are calling my name.

48
00:03:10,308 --> 00:03:12,414
I said they're not calling upon the injured.

49
00:03:13,070 --> 00:03:17,284
He replied: They are calling upon the Ansaar(أنصار), and I'm one of them,

50
00:03:17,635 --> 00:03:20,567
and I will respond to the call, even if I would have to crawl.

51
00:03:21,833 --> 00:03:27,743
He then put on his sword and went into the battle field and fought until, his left arm was cut off from the shoulder.

52
00:03:27,775 --> 00:03:28,870
I said: Abu Aqeel(أبوعقيل)!

53
00:03:29,576 --> 00:03:31,053
He responded with a weak tongue.

54
00:03:32,053 --> 00:03:32,917
By saying: Yes!

55
00:03:33,512 --> 00:03:34,026
Who won.

56
00:03:34,637 --> 00:03:37,024
I said: Rejoice! The enemy of Allah was killed.

57
00:03:37,899 --> 00:03:40,828
He raised his finger upwards and praised Allah and then he died.

58
00:03:41,740 --> 00:03:43,375
I told my father Umar(عُمَر) about that,

59
00:03:43,510 --> 00:03:48,326
He said: May Allah have mercy on him, he persisted in search of martyrdom until he got it.

60
00:03:49,285 --> 00:03:50,682
This is in Al-Waqedi(ألواقعدي).

61
00:03:53,191 --> 00:03:56,257
Salim(سالم) the servant of Abu Hudhaifa(أبوحذيفة) was told

62
00:03:56,305 --> 00:04:00,803
that if he feared you wouldn't be capable of carrying the banner during the battle.

63
00:04:01,302 --> 00:04:03,199
It could be transferred to someone else.

64
00:04:04,111 --> 00:04:08,203
To understand the role of the Banner had,

65
00:04:08,306 --> 00:04:18,334
in those days, obviously without having loudspeakers and walkie talkies and internal radio between the soldiers,

66
00:04:19,811 --> 00:04:26,191
they had to invent ways of sticking together, because the army needs to have some central command.

67
00:04:26,690 --> 00:04:28,944
You can't just have a bunch of people fighting on their own.

68
00:04:29,753 --> 00:04:32,013
There needs to be some unity and cohesion.

69
00:04:33,077 --> 00:04:38,584
What happens is, the army would be split into small groups every group would have a leader.

70
00:04:40,219 --> 00:04:46,798
And then the entire army or, if the army is big, it would be divided into flanks, or battalions,

71
00:04:47,037 --> 00:04:51,481
and each battalion would have a banner, a banner is a flag.

72
00:04:52,805 --> 00:04:55,633
And if you had more than one maybe they would have different colors.

73
00:04:57,725 --> 00:05:00,535
When the soldier is the midst of fighting,

74
00:05:02,310 --> 00:05:06,244
and he wants to know where his brother's are, he would look up and try to find where the banner is.

75
00:05:07,149 --> 00:05:08,554
That's where you know where your people are.

76
00:05:09,617 --> 00:05:15,720
So that is your post that you keep on looking for throughout the battle,

77
00:05:16,498 --> 00:05:21,685
because you know the dust is rising and swords are on top of your head, you could be disoriented.

78
00:05:22,823 --> 00:05:24,578
You wouldn't know which direction is which.

79
00:05:25,270 --> 00:05:28,575
So you look up to try to find where your banner is

80
00:05:29,219 --> 00:05:34,688
also, when you look up, you always want to see the banner there,

81
00:05:35,148 --> 00:05:37,528
because if it's not there, that's bad news.

82
00:05:38,235 --> 00:05:39,757
It means that your army has been defeated.

83
00:05:40,866 --> 00:05:45,872
The most important part of the army, is where the banner is.

84
00:05:46,362 --> 00:05:48,868
And the carrier of the banner is playing the most important part.

85
00:05:50,173 --> 00:05:54,346
Therefore, having that banner up and straight all the time

86
00:05:54,481 --> 00:06:00,216
is extremely important for the morale of the army and for the progress of fighting itself.

87
00:06:01,089 --> 00:06:06,081
I mean, whenever the soldier looks up and doesn't find the banner, that's it the soldier loses hope and just runs away.

88
00:06:07,194 --> 00:06:08,330
 There's nothing else to fight for.

89
00:06:09,354 --> 00:06:17,196
So, Salim(سالم) was, the servant of Hudhaifa(حذيفة).

90
00:06:17,712 --> 00:06:23,188
He was the one charged with the responsibility of carrying the banner.

91
00:06:23,881 --> 00:06:26,389
So they told him: Are up for it.

92
00:06:26,722 --> 00:06:27,246
Can he do it.?

93
00:06:27,627 --> 00:06:33,261
He said: I am the worst carrier of Qur'an, if that happened.

94
00:06:35,237 --> 00:06:38,314
If I fail you, I am the worst carrier of Qur'an.

95
00:06:40,313 --> 00:06:45,250
And this shows you that their understanding of carrying Qur'an means that you have to live by Qur'an

96
00:06:45,401 --> 00:06:49,528
I mean how could I be a hafiz(حافظ) of the Qur'an and then allow that banner to fall from my hands.

97
00:06:52,986 --> 00:06:56,133
So his right hand was chopped he then carried the banner with his left hand.

98
00:06:57,141 --> 00:06:58,538
His left hand was later cut,

99
00:06:59,046 --> 00:07:02,879
so he embraced the banner with what was left of his both arms, reciting,

100
00:07:03,371 --> 00:07:10,607
وَما مُحَمَّدٌ إِلّا رَسولٌ قَد خَلَت مِن قَبلِهِ الرُّسُلُ ۚ

101
00:07:11,024 --> 00:07:17,378
أَفَإِن ماتَ أَو قُتِلَ انقَلَبتُم عَلىٰ أَعقابِكُم ۚ

102
00:07:17,657 --> 00:07:24,466
وَمَن يَنقَلِب عَلىٰ عَقِبَيهِ فَلَن يَضُرَّ اللَّهَ شَيئًا ۗ

103
00:07:24,754 --> 00:07:28,318
وَسَيَجزِي اللَّهُ الشّاكِرينَ۞

104
00:07:28,593 --> 00:07:36,924
وَما كانَ لِنَفسٍ أَن تَموتَ إِلّا بِإِذنِ اللَّهِ كِتابًا مُؤَجَّلًا ۗ

105
00:07:37,340 --> 00:07:46,953
وَمَن يُرِد ثَوابَ الدُّنيا نُؤتِهِ مِنها وَمَن يُرِد ثَوابَ الآخِرَةِ نُؤتِهِ مِنها ۚ

106
00:07:47,374 --> 00:07:50,752
وَسَنَجزِي الشّاكِرينَ۞

107
00:07:50,988 --> 00:07:59,642
وَكَأَيِّن مِن نَبِيٍّ قاتَلَ مَعَهُ رِبِّيّونَ كَثيرٌ فَما وَهَنوا

108
00:08:00,057 --> 00:08:08,484
فَما وَهَنوا لِما أَصابَهُم في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ وَما ضَعُفوا وَمَا استَكانوا ۗ

109
00:08:08,928 --> 00:08:13,952
وَاللَّهُ يُحِبُّ الصّابِرينَ۞

110
00:08:14,396 --> 00:08:18,411
Muhammad(محمد) is not but a messenger, other messengers have passed on before him.

111
00:08:18,961 --> 00:08:21,599
So if he were to die or be killed.

112
00:08:22,073 --> 00:08:24,876
Would you turn your back on your heels,

113
00:08:25,400 --> 00:08:29,535
and who turns back on his heels will never harm Allah at all.

114
00:08:30,027 --> 00:08:31,362
but Allah will reward the grateful,

115
00:08:31,630 --> 00:08:33,163
Al-Imran(ألعمران) Verse 144.

116
00:08:34,709 --> 00:08:41,324
And then he recited and how many a prophet fought, and with him fight many religious scholars,

117
00:08:42,649 --> 00:08:50,985
وَكَأَيِّن مِن نَبِيٍّ قاتَلَ مَعَهُ رِبِّيّونَ كَثيرٌ فَما وَهَنوا لِما أَصابَهُم في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ وَما ضَعُفوا وَمَا استَكانوا

118
00:08:51,159 --> 00:08:54,723
But they never lost assurance due to what afflicted them in the Cause of Allah,

119
00:08:55,119 --> 00:08:57,897
nor did they weaken or submit, and Allah loves the steadfast,

120
00:08:58,127 --> 00:08:59,366
Al-Imran(ألعمران) verse 146.

121
00:09:00,461 --> 00:09:03,670
When he was about to die, he asked his companions what happened to Abu Hudhaifa(أبوحذيفة).

122
00:09:04,839 --> 00:09:05,704
They said: He was killed.

123
00:09:06,474 --> 00:09:09,505
He then asked them about another person they responded that he was also killed.

124
00:09:10,171 --> 00:09:12,382
He said: Then bury me between the two of them,

125
00:09:13,972 --> 00:09:15,655
that's narrated by Ibn Al-Mubarak(إبن المبارك).

126
00:09:17,266 --> 00:09:18,344
Zaid Ibn Sabat(زيد إبن ثابت) said:

127
00:09:19,035 --> 00:09:24,307
On the day of Uhud the Messenger of Allah sent me to look for Saad Ibn Rabiya(سعد إبن ربيعة).

128
00:09:25,368 --> 00:09:29,504
And if I find him, to deliver the Salaams(سلام) of the Messenger of Allah to him.

129
00:09:30,242 --> 00:09:35,829
So I found him among the bodies of the dead pronouncing his last moments with around 70 injuries in his body.

130
00:09:37,020 --> 00:09:39,868
I told him the Messenger of Allah delivers his Salaams(سلام) to you.

131
00:09:40,622 --> 00:09:44,867
He said: Salaams(سلام) to the Rasool of Allah and Salaams(سلام) to you.

132
00:09:45,765 --> 00:09:49,352
Tell the Messenger of Allah that I am now smelling the scent of paradise

133
00:09:50,662 --> 00:09:53,608
and tell my people the Ansaar(أنصار) that you have no excuse,

134
00:09:54,073 --> 00:09:57,748
if the Messenger of Allah is harmed while there is still an eye blinking among you.

135
00:09:58,788 --> 00:09:59,738
After that he died.

136
00:10:00,755 --> 00:10:02,569
This is Sahih(صحيح) narration.

137
00:10:04,388 --> 00:10:10,330
Ibn Mubarak(إبن المبارك) narrates that he passed by a man on the day of the Battle of the bridge

138
00:10:10,965 --> 00:10:15,195
with his arms and legs cut off while he was crawling and reciting,

139
00:10:15,568 --> 00:10:25,007
وَمَن يُطِعِ اللَّهَ وَالرَّسولَ فَأُولٰئِكَ مَعَ الَّذينَ أَنعَمَ اللَّهُ عَلَيهِم

140
00:10:25,434 --> 00:10:37,192
مَعَ الَّذينَ أَنعَمَ اللَّهُ عَلَيهِم مِنَ النَّبِيّينَ وَالصِّدّيقينَ وَالشُّهَداءِ وَالصّالِحينَ ۚ

141
00:10:37,714 --> 00:10:41,307
وَحَسُنَ أُولٰئِكَ رَفيقًا۞

142
00:10:41,650 --> 00:10:43,763
And whoever obeys Allah and the messenger,

143
00:10:44,110 --> 00:10:50,159
those will be with the ones, upon whom Allah has bestowed favor of the prophets

144
00:10:50,279 --> 00:10:54,763
and the steadfast affirmers of truth, the martyrs, the righteous,

145
00:10:55,667 --> 00:10:59,076
مِنَ النَّبِيّينَ وَالصِّدّيقينَ وَالشُّهَداءِ وَالصّالِحينَ ۚ وَحَسُنَ أُولٰئِكَ رَفيقًا۞

146
00:11:00,361 --> 00:11:04,012
 Someone asked him: Who are you? He replied, I am one of the Ansaar(ألأنْصَار).

147
00:11:04,615 --> 00:11:09,018
Abu Hasan Al-Marwardi(أبوالحسن ألمروردي) narrated that Ali bin Abi Bakr(علي بن أبي بكر) said:

148
00:11:09,832 --> 00:11:17,333
I've seen a Muslim in a battle against the Romans, with his intestines spilled in front of him over his saddle.

149
00:11:18,190 --> 00:11:22,967
He stuck them back to his stomach and tied around his turban, and he carried on fighting.

150
00:11:23,880 --> 00:11:28,993
His Guts was pulling out, put them back, tied turban and carried on fighting.

151
00:11:30,603 --> 00:11:34,417
And he ended up killing over 10 Roman soldiers before he fell down dead.

152
00:11:35,489 --> 00:11:36,235
CHAPTER SEVEN,

153
00:11:36,790 --> 00:11:39,735
the virtues of killing an infidels for the sake of Allah,

154
00:11:40,671 --> 00:11:44,398
Allah says, Surah Muhammad(سورةمحمد).

155
00:11:44,752 --> 00:11:56,641
فَإِذا لَقيتُمُ الَّذينَ كَفَروا فَضَربَ الرِّقابِ حَتّىٰ إِذا أَثخَنتُموهُم فَشُدُّوا الوَثاقَ

156
00:11:57,173 --> 00:12:06,755
فَإِمّا مَنًّا بَعدُ وَإِمّا فِداءً حَتّىٰ تَضَعَ الحَربُ أَوزارَها ۚ

157
00:12:07,275 --> 00:12:12,788
ذٰلِكَ وَلَو يَشاءُ اللَّهُ لَانتَصَرَ مِنهُم

158
00:12:13,153 --> 00:12:17,020
وَلٰكِن لِيَبلُوَ بَعضَكُم بِبَعضٍ ۗ

159
00:12:17,209 --> 00:12:23,785
وَالَّذينَ قُتِلوا في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ فَلَن يُضِلَّ أَعمالَهُم۞

160
00:12:24,338 --> 00:12:28,495
So when you meet those, who disbelieve in battle, strike their necks.

161
00:12:31,220 --> 00:12:33,700
Abu Hurairah(أبوهريرة) narrated the Messenger of Allah said:

162
00:12:34,077 --> 00:12:39,173
The non believer, and the one, who kills him will not be joined together and hellfire.

163
00:12:40,149 --> 00:12:43,211
لا يجمع الله بين كافر وقاتلهم

164
00:12:43,742 --> 00:12:44,849
This is in Sahih Muslim(صحيح مسلم).

165
00:12:45,154 --> 00:12:49,088
In other words, the Muslim is so rewarded for killing the non believers

166
00:12:49,171 --> 00:12:53,588
to the extent that Allah will never dishonor the Muslim by joining him with the Kafir(كافر) in hellfire.

167
00:12:54,644 --> 00:13:00,944
I mean if you cut for him a one way ticket to Jahannum(جَهَّنَّم), be assured that you will get a one way ticket to Jannah(جنة).

168
00:13:02,825 --> 00:13:03,610
He takes your place.

169
00:13:04,706 --> 00:13:06,951
He takes your place in Jahannum(جَهَّنَّم).

170
00:13:07,768 --> 00:13:09,628
Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك) he heard his brother Al-Bara(ألبراء)

171
00:13:09,668 --> 00:13:13,787
and Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك), and his brother were two different personalities, even though they're brothers.

172
00:13:15,756 --> 00:13:17,724
Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك), was more of a scholar,

173
00:13:18,517 --> 00:13:25,350
and Al-Bara Bin Malik(ألبراء بن مالك) was more of… Yani(يعني) is a Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) is an understatement.

174
00:13:29,286 --> 00:13:32,154
Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك) heard his brother Al-Bara(ألبراء) humming poetry,

175
00:13:32,218 --> 00:13:34,569
so he told him: O my brother you're humming poetry.?

176
00:13:35,206 --> 00:13:39,839
What if this is the last thing you speak, if you die, and these are your last words,

177
00:13:40,976 --> 00:13:43,661
because for Sahabah(صحابه), the Qur'an replaced poetry.

178
00:13:45,304 --> 00:13:49,151
So, Al-Bara(ألبراء) said: No!

179
00:13:49,558 --> 00:13:54,599
Let me read, when Qur'an was real the Sahabah(صحابه) disliked reciting anything,

180
00:13:54,810 --> 00:13:58,812
by the way anything between brackets are my words, they're not Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس).

181
00:13:59,643 --> 00:14:02,691
We have brackets, these are my illustrations,

182
00:14:03,397 --> 00:14:06,981
when Qur'an was revealed the Sahabah(صحابه) disliked reciting everything but Qur'an

183
00:14:07,053 --> 00:14:12,675
Anas(أنس) was warning his brother in saying that if you die, this moment and the last words you spoke were lines of poetry.

184
00:14:13,321 --> 00:14:14,297
How would you face Allah.?

185
00:14:15,226 --> 00:14:17,559
In another narration, he told him: To rather remember Allah.

186
00:14:17,964 --> 00:14:18,929
Al-Bara(ألبراء) said: No!

187
00:14:19,501 --> 00:14:21,620
A man like me won't die on his bed.

188
00:14:22,200 --> 00:14:25,265
I've killed 99 of the non believers and hypocrites.

189
00:14:27,051 --> 00:14:28,853
Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك) told him: This might be the last thing you would say

190
00:14:28,925 --> 00:14:32,917
He said: Don't worry for somebody like me, will die in the battlefield In Sha Allah(إنْ شاءالله).

191
00:14:33,274 --> 00:14:34,836
I've killed 99 Kuffar(كفار).

192
00:14:37,094 --> 00:14:42,394
Umar(عُمَر) wrote to his military generals to never allow Al-Bara(ألبراء) to hold any position of leadership in the Muslim armies.

193
00:14:43,347 --> 00:14:47,218
A complete bane across the board.

194
00:14:47,869 --> 00:14:50,930
The reason Umar(عُمَر) said: He is too hazardous for the Muslims,

195
00:14:51,512 --> 00:14:54,067
مهلك من المهال

196
00:14:57,487 --> 00:15:00,263
During the battle against the forces of Musaylimah(مسيلمة) the liar.

197
00:15:00,916 --> 00:15:06,508
He sat on a shield and asked the Muslims to carry the shield on their spears and throw him over the walls.

198
00:15:06,658 --> 00:15:07,706
This was his elevator,

199
00:15:09,008 --> 00:15:12,325
sit on the shield, carried on the spears, to open the gates,

200
00:15:12,421 --> 00:15:15,433
he did open the gates but after he received over 80 injuries.

201
00:15:16,215 --> 00:15:17,322
And that's in Al-Osaba(أثابة).

202
00:15:18,780 --> 00:15:20,809
Anas(أنس) narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:

203
00:15:21,184 --> 00:15:27,486
There might be a man with disheveled hair, dusty clothes, who no one gives attention to.

204
00:15:28,025 --> 00:15:30,865
But if he makes an oath, Allah will fulfill it for him.

205
00:15:31,730 --> 00:15:33,109
One of them is Al-Bara Bin Malik(ألبراء بن مالك).

206
00:15:34,342 --> 00:15:39,447
Now people would disregard this person, but if this person says Wallah(ولله) this would happen,

207
00:15:39,818 --> 00:15:43,851
Allah would fulfill his word, he's very close to Allah.

208
00:15:44,279 --> 00:15:46,279
This is in At-Tirmidhi(ألتِّرمِذِيْ) and Al Hakim(ألحَاكِم).

209
00:15:46,351 --> 00:15:52,229
So on the day of the Battle of Tastur(تستر) the Muslims asked the Al-Bara(ألبراء) to make an oath to give them victory,

210
00:15:52,689 --> 00:15:59,856
Al-Bara(ألبراء) said: O Allah, I make an oath that you hand us over their shoulders, and to make me follow Your prophet.

211
00:16:01,035 --> 00:16:04,155
He then charged the enemy and the Muslims follow them, the Persian lost.

212
00:16:04,694 --> 00:16:06,973
And the Al-Bara(ألبراء) was martyred and Allah fulfilled his oath.

213
00:16:08,258 --> 00:16:12,216
Anas(أنس) narrated, when Abu Musa(أبوموسى) was appointed governor of Al-Basra(ألبصرة).

214
00:16:13,179 --> 00:16:17,301
He told Al-Bara(ألبراء), to choose any position of leadership in his government, not in Jihad(جهاد),

215
00:16:17,922 --> 00:16:20,703
in this government, and he will be appointed to it.

216
00:16:21,336 --> 00:16:23,317
Al-Bara(ألبراء) said: I don't want any.

217
00:16:23,897 --> 00:16:31,269
Rather, I want you to hand me over my bow horse spear sword and shield, and then send me to Jihad(جهاد).

218
00:16:32,271 --> 00:16:34,952
He sent him in an army Al-Bara(ألبراء) was the first to die.

219
00:16:35,880 --> 00:16:37,214
So it's a battle Tastur(تستر).

220
00:16:38,190 --> 00:16:41,944
Anas(أنس) narrated the Messenger of Allah said: On the day of the Battle of hunain(حنين).

221
00:16:42,404 --> 00:16:49,104
Whoever kills a non-believer can loot him Abu Talha(أبوطلحة) killed on that day 20 of the non believers and looted them all,

222
00:16:50,461 --> 00:16:52,102
Abu Daud(أبوداؤد) and Al Hakim(ألحَاكِم).

223
00:17:01,024 --> 00:17:01,579
CHAPTER EIGHT:

224
00:17:02,436 --> 00:17:10,214
The virtue of an individual or a small group, immersing themselves within a large army of non believers

225
00:17:10,433 --> 00:17:13,414
in search of martyrdom and causing damage to the enemy.

226
00:17:15,480 --> 00:17:18,160
This chapter can be used as an evidence for what?

227
00:17:19,921 --> 00:17:20,996
Amleat Ish'haadiah(عمليات ألشهادية),

228
00:17:21,065 --> 00:17:29,626
the whole chapter, you could reword it as the Tahseen(تحسين) legalization of Amleat Ish'haadiah(عمليات ألشهادية).

229
00:17:30,150 --> 00:17:34,511
 Amleat Ish'haadiah(عمليات ألشهادية), martyrdom operations, martyrdom operations.

230
00:17:35,507 --> 00:17:36,290
Allah says,

231
00:17:36,787 --> 00:17:46,276
فَلَمّا فَصَلَ طالوتُ بِالجُنودِ قالَ إِنَّ اللَّهَ مُبتَليكُم بِنَهَرٍ

232
00:17:47,165 --> 00:17:55,818
فَمَن شَرِبَ مِنهُ فَلَيسَ مِنّي وَمَن لَم يَطعَمهُ فَإِنَّهُ مِنّي

233
00:17:56,580 --> 00:18:00,715
إِلّا مَنِ اغتَرَفَ غُرفَةً بِيَدِهِ ۚ

234
00:18:01,144 --> 00:18:05,424
فَشَرِبوا مِنهُ إِلّا قَليلًا مِنهُم ۚ

235
00:18:05,962 --> 00:18:12,217
فَلَمّا جاوَزَهُ هُوَ وَالَّذينَ آمَنوا مَعَهُ قالو

236
00:18:12,772 --> 00:18:18,214
قالوا لا طاقَةَ لَنَا اليَومَ بِجالوتَ وَجُنودِهِ ۚ

237
00:18:18,881 --> 00:18:30,605
قالَ الَّذينَ يَظُنّونَ أَنَّهُم مُلاقُو اللَّهِ كَم مِن فِئَةٍ قَليلَةٍ غَلَبَت

238
00:18:31,343 --> 00:18:40,429
كَم مِن فِئَةٍ قَليلَةٍ غَلَبَت فِئَةً كَثيرَةً بِإِذنِ اللَّهِ ۗ

239
00:18:41,058 --> 00:18:44,235
وَاللَّهُ مَعَ الصّابِرينَ۞

240
00:18:45,157 --> 00:18:47,542
But those who are certain that they would meet Allah said,

241
00:18:47,987 --> 00:18:51,959
how many a small company has overcome a large company by permission of Allah.

242
00:18:52,391 --> 00:18:57,504
فِئَةٍ قَليلَةٍ غَلَبَت فِئَةً كَثيرَةً بِإِذنِ اللَّهِ ۗ وَاللَّهُ مَعَ الصّابِرينَ۞

243
00:18:57,591 --> 00:18:58,869
And Allah is with the patient.

244
00:18:59,718 --> 00:19:00,535
Allah says,

245
00:19:01,955 --> 00:19:14,667
وَمِنَ النّاسِ مَن يَشري نَفسَهُ ابتِغاءَ مَرضاتِ اللَّهِ ۗ وَاللَّهُ رَءوفٌ بِالعِبادِ۞

246
00:19:15,021 --> 00:19:21,354
and up the people is he, who sells himself, seeking means to the approval of Allah.

247
00:19:23,299 --> 00:19:24,815
And Allah is kind to his servants.

248
00:19:24,902 --> 00:19:27,498
وَمِنَ النّاسِ مَن يَشري نَفسَهُ ابتِغاءَ مَرضاتِ اللَّهِ ۗ

249
00:19:29,284 --> 00:19:32,176
So, here you have a person who is selling himself to get the pleasure of Allah.

250
00:19:33,533 --> 00:19:34,652
Mudrik Ibn Auf(مدرك إبن عوف) said:

251
00:19:35,541 --> 00:19:40,866
I was with Umar(عُمَر), when he received the messenger from An-Nouman Bin Makran(ألنعمان بن مقرن),

252
00:19:41,144 --> 00:19:43,565
Umar(عُمَر) asked him about the condition of the soldiers,

253
00:19:44,052 --> 00:19:47,925
the messenger kept on mentioning to Umar(عُمَر), some of the well known people who died, and then he said:

254
00:19:48,734 --> 00:19:50,496
And others died, whom I don't know.

255
00:19:51,147 --> 00:19:52,504
Umar(عُمَر) said: But Allah knows them.

256
00:19:53,186 --> 00:19:56,583
The messenger said: And men who sold themselves to Allah,

257
00:19:57,718 --> 00:20:03,932
Mudrik(مدرك) said: Among those is my uncle people claim he killed himself by throwing himself into the enemy's army.

258
00:20:04,567 --> 00:20:07,186
 Umar(عُمَر) said: Whoever claims that, is a liar.

259
00:20:07,662 --> 00:20:10,399
He is one of those, who sold this world for the next.

260
00:20:11,185 --> 00:20:12,891
Thus is in Al-Musannaf(ألمصنف) and it is Sahih(صحيح).

261
00:20:13,581 --> 00:20:19,564
So, here you have a man, who jumps into the army, seeking martyrdom.

262
00:20:21,201 --> 00:20:24,083
Might as well just put on an explosive belt, what's the difference.

263
00:20:25,118 --> 00:20:31,253
Jumping in an army of 1000s, so it's a definite death.

264
00:20:33,107 --> 00:20:38,297
A battalion of non believers came from the east, and was met by a man from the Ansaar(أنصار),

265
00:20:38,740 --> 00:20:44,073
he charged against them alone and penetrated their ranks until they came out from the other side of the battalion.

266
00:20:44,716 --> 00:20:48,305
Then he charged them from the back and broke the ranks, until it came out from the front,

267
00:20:48,976 --> 00:20:52,532
he repeated that two or three times zigzagging in the army.

268
00:20:52,937 --> 00:20:55,433
Saad Ibn Hisham(سعد إبن هشام) mentioned that to Abu Hurairah(أبوهريرة).

269
00:20:55,814 --> 00:20:56,996
Abu Hurairah(أبوهريرة) recited:

270
00:20:57,417 --> 00:21:02,218
And of the people is he, who sells himself, seeking means to approval of Allah.

271
00:21:02,845 --> 00:21:04,704
And Allah is kind to His servants.

272
00:21:05,990 --> 00:21:08,458
Aslam Abi Amran(أسلم أبي عمران) said:

273
00:21:08,498 --> 00:21:13,939
We were in the army heading from Madina, heading towards Constantinople,

274
00:21:14,471 --> 00:21:17,161
the head of the army was Abdur Rahman Bin Khalid Bin Walid(عبدالرحمن بن خالدبن وليد).

275
00:21:18,082 --> 00:21:20,693
The Romans had their backs facing the gates of the city.

276
00:21:21,502 --> 00:21:23,638
One among us rushed alone towards them.

277
00:21:23,701 --> 00:21:26,985
Some people said there is no God but Allah, He is throwing himself into destruction.

278
00:21:27,065 --> 00:21:28,660
تُلقوا بِأَيديكُم إِلَى التَّهلُكَةِ ۛ

279
00:21:29,636 --> 00:21:31,034
Abu Ayub Al-Ansari(أبو أيوب ألأنصاري) said:

280
00:21:31,143 --> 00:21:33,725
This verse was revealed speaking about us, the Ansaar(أنصار).

281
00:21:34,401 --> 00:21:37,121
When Allah gave His Messenger victory and Islam prevailed.

282
00:21:37,656 --> 00:21:40,579
We said: Let's go back to our businesses and take care of it.

283
00:21:41,008 --> 00:21:42,444
Allah then revealed the verse,

284
00:21:42,817 --> 00:21:50,465
وَأَنفِقوا في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ وَلا تُلقوا بِأَيديكُم إِلَى التَّهلُكَةِ ۛ

285
00:21:50,944 --> 00:21:57,233
وَأَحسِنوا ۛ إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ المُحسِنينَ۞

286
00:21:57,862 --> 00:22:05,257
And spend in the way of Allah and do not throw yourselves with your own hands into destruction, and do good.

287
00:22:05,614 --> 00:22:07,692
Indeed, Allah loves the doers of good.

288
00:22:08,470 --> 00:22:14,575
So throwing ourselves into the destruction meant going back to our farms and businesses, leaving Jihad(جهاد).

289
00:22:15,564 --> 00:22:20,265
Abu Amran(أبوعمران) said Abu Ayub(أبوأيوب) remained in Jihad(جهاد), until he was buried in Constantinople,

290
00:22:21,749 --> 00:22:23,796
 it is in Abu Daud(أبوداؤد), At-Tirmidhi(ألتِّرمِذِيْ) and Al Hakim(ألحَاكِم).

291
00:22:26,625 --> 00:22:27,720
Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) said:

292
00:22:28,347 --> 00:22:34,908
The Messenger of Allah sent only two men, Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود) and Khabbab(خباب) as an army

293
00:22:35,289 --> 00:22:37,493
and he sent the Dahya(دحية) as an army alone.

294
00:22:38,694 --> 00:22:41,855
He said: Dahya(دحية), as an army by himself, it's one man.

295
00:22:42,503 --> 00:22:43,694
This is in Al-Sunan Al-Kubra(ألسنن ألكبرى).

296
00:22:44,932 --> 00:22:45,789
As-Shafie(ألشَّافعي) said:

297
00:22:46,789 --> 00:22:52,256
One of the Ansaar(أنصار) was late behind when the killing of the Sahabah(صحابه) next to the well of Mauna(ماعونة) took place.

298
00:22:53,201 --> 00:22:56,972
By the time he arrived vultures are already devouring his companions.

299
00:22:57,634 --> 00:22:58,857
He told the Amr Bin Umayah(عمرو بن أمية).

300
00:22:59,714 --> 00:23:03,706
I'm going to go alone and face the enemy, so they can kill me.

301
00:23:04,539 --> 00:23:07,532
I don't want to be left behind when our companions are killed.

302
00:23:09,493 --> 00:23:12,501
When our companions were killed, he did, and he was killed.

303
00:23:13,080 --> 00:23:15,967
So, here you see that is Yani(يعني).

304
00:23:16,483 --> 00:23:21,351
He says: I'm going to go alone and face the enemy so they can kill me.

305
00:23:21,602 --> 00:23:23,862
He's going for what purpose, to die.

306
00:23:25,066 --> 00:23:26,335
He made his intentions clear.

307
00:23:27,073 --> 00:23:29,716
He didn't say I'm going to kill them even though that was part of his attention,

308
00:23:29,756 --> 00:23:30,798
but he said: I'm going to die.

309
00:23:31,535 --> 00:23:34,637
And then he said: I don't want to be left behind when our companions were killed.

310
00:23:35,467 --> 00:23:36,301
I want to join them.

311
00:23:37,063 --> 00:23:38,531
He did, and he was killed.

312
00:23:38,926 --> 00:23:43,158
When Amr Bin Umayah(عمرو بن أمية) the only survivor of the incident told the Messenger of Allah about what happened.

313
00:23:44,468 --> 00:23:47,208
The Messenger of Allah said, good words about the man,

314
00:23:47,692 --> 00:23:49,169
and then he told Amr Bin Umayah(عمرو بن أمية).

315
00:23:49,494 --> 00:23:51,707
And why didn't you go ahead with him.?

316
00:23:53,540 --> 00:23:54,794
Why didn't he go ahead with him.?

317
00:23:56,334 --> 00:24:02,774
See this issue of martyrdom operations has became a controversial issue when it shouldn't,

318
00:24:06,078 --> 00:24:08,687
because the difference between suicide and martyrdom is clear.

319
00:24:09,155 --> 00:24:11,382
The difference between suicide and martyrdom is Niyah(نية).

320
00:24:13,203 --> 00:24:16,378
It's the Niyah(نية) that makes it suicide or makes it martyrdom.

321
00:24:18,854 --> 00:24:21,003
And the man, who was in the middle of the battlefield,

322
00:24:21,305 --> 00:24:21,527
Right!

323
00:24:21,615 --> 00:24:25,846
The middle of the battlefield, and he stepped over his so to kill himself.

324
00:24:26,640 --> 00:24:29,886
Even though he was fighting that was considered to be suicide

325
00:24:29,949 --> 00:24:32,820
and Rasool Allah ﷺ when he heard Shaheed(شَهِيد), he is Shaheed(شَهِيد).

326
00:24:33,193 --> 00:24:34,416
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: He's not.

327
00:24:35,170 --> 00:24:35,828
He's in An-Naar(ألنَّار).

328
00:24:38,123 --> 00:24:43,058
What made him die in the battlefield, and it was considered to be suicide is because of his Niyah(نية),

329
00:24:43,272 --> 00:24:48,592
he couldn't have patience, because of the pain he was going through, he was injured.

330
00:24:48,892 --> 00:24:54,099
He didn't have patience, he stuck a sword in the ground, and he jumped over it, and committed suicide.

331
00:24:56,836 --> 00:25:01,833
This Shaheed(شَهِيد) who goes and blows himself up.

332
00:25:02,381 --> 00:25:05,001
When he goes to blow himself up, is his intention to kill himself.?

333
00:25:06,094 --> 00:25:07,401
His intention is to kill the enemy.

334
00:25:07,710 --> 00:25:09,837
That's why he went otherwise he would blow himself up in his house.

335
00:25:10,076 --> 00:25:11,437
Why didn't he have to go among the enemy.

336
00:25:12,539 --> 00:25:17,136
He's doing it among the enemy to kill the enemy, and he is dying as a byproduct of that.

337
00:25:18,485 --> 00:25:22,906
And his intention was to make Nikaya(نكاية) in the ranks of the enemy.

338
00:25:22,969 --> 00:25:24,549
So, how come the two are confused.

339
00:25:25,461 --> 00:25:27,889
It should be no room for confusion, it's very clear issue.

340
00:25:29,024 --> 00:25:31,556
The difference between Shahadah(شهادة) and suicide is the Niyah(نية).

341
00:25:32,880 --> 00:25:39,514
Somebody who has committed suicide, commits suicide because they're not happy with the Qadar(قَدَر) of Allah.

342
00:25:40,053 --> 00:25:43,661
They're not happy with their latten life, they lost hope.

343
00:25:44,823 --> 00:25:47,459
They're in the state of despair, so they take away their life.

344
00:25:48,260 --> 00:25:50,609
Ash-Shaheed(ألشَهِيد) is doing it to please Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ

345
00:25:51,070 --> 00:25:53,217
taking away your life for a worldly reason is suicide,

346
00:25:53,558 --> 00:25:59,098
taking away your life for the sake of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ to please Him, is Shahadah(شَهَادَة), that's the difference between the two.

347
00:26:01,796 --> 00:26:04,184
Yazid Ibn Abi Ubaid(يزيد إبن أبي عبيد) said:

348
00:26:04,351 --> 00:26:05,878
I asked Salmah Ibn Akwah(سلمة إبن أكوع)

349
00:26:06,354 --> 00:26:09,341
What was your pledge to the Messenger of Allah on the day of Hudaibiyah(حديبية)?

350
00:26:09,381 --> 00:26:10,664
He said: We pledged to die,

351
00:26:11,492 --> 00:26:12,597
تبيعنا على الموت

352
00:26:12,714 --> 00:26:13,849
The pledge was to die

353
00:26:13,889 --> 00:26:15,020
and this is in Bukhari(بخاريْ) and Muslim(ألمسلم),

354
00:26:15,429 --> 00:26:16,397
the Messenger of Allah said:

355
00:26:16,786 --> 00:26:22,747
A time will come when the best of my mankind would be a man holding on to the bridle of his horse in the sake of Allah,

356
00:26:23,081 --> 00:26:27,767
whenever he hears a call to battle he mounts his horse and searches for death.

357
00:26:29,176 --> 00:26:32,256
So he's searching for death but he's doing it for the sake of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

358
00:26:32,716 --> 00:26:34,819
Ibn Masood(إبن مسعود) narrated the Messenger of Allah said:

359
00:26:35,517 --> 00:26:37,255
Allah is amazed with two men.

360
00:26:37,969 --> 00:26:41,692
One of them is a man who woke up from his comfortable bed to pray,

361
00:26:42,168 --> 00:26:45,280
eager to receive the reward from Allah, and fearing His punishment.

362
00:26:45,947 --> 00:26:48,928
The second man is one, who went to fight in the path of Allah,

363
00:26:49,296 --> 00:26:51,939
but this company turned their backs in the battlefield,

364
00:26:52,526 --> 00:26:55,318
he realized the punishment of turning ones back in battle,

365
00:26:55,957 --> 00:26:57,600
and the reward of being steadfast.

366
00:26:58,322 --> 00:27:01,087
So he went back to fight in order to have his blood spilled,

367
00:27:01,616 --> 00:27:02,471
Allah would say:

368
00:27:02,772 --> 00:27:08,185
Look at this servant of Mine, he went back to fight, eager for what I will reward him,

369
00:27:08,471 --> 00:27:11,252
and fearing my punishment, until his blood was spilled,

370
00:27:11,419 --> 00:27:13,808
and this is in Ahmad(أحمد) and it is Sahih(صحيح).

371
00:27:14,419 --> 00:27:15,244
Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) says:

372
00:27:15,284 --> 00:27:20,564
If there weren't any Hadith(حديث) on the virtue of immersing oneself in the enemy's army then this Hadith(حديث),

373
00:27:21,120 --> 00:27:22,112
it would have been sufficient.

374
00:27:25,056 --> 00:27:27,390
Before I get into the story of Salmah Ibn Akwah(سلمة إبن أكوع).

375
00:27:27,620 --> 00:27:36,034
Let's make my comments after that, I'll just go through the story, it's a bit long story, but it's a very interesting one.

376
00:27:36,724 --> 00:27:40,175
Salmah Ibn Akwah(سلمة إبن أكوع) narrates and he's telling his own story and this is in Sahih Muslim(صحيح مسلم).

377
00:27:42,273 --> 00:27:46,372
He said: Then we moved, returning to Madina and halter at a place

378
00:27:47,316 --> 00:27:51,067
where there was a mountain between us and Banul-Lahyan(بنوالَّحيان), who were polytheist.

379
00:27:51,155 --> 00:27:53,335
He's talking about Banul-Lahyan(بنوالَّحيان), who were polytheists,

380
00:27:54,274 --> 00:28:00,887
the Messenger of Allah, may peace be upon him, asked Allah's forgiveness for one, who ascended the mountain at night

381
00:28:01,001 --> 00:28:05,835
 to act as a scout for the messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions.

382
00:28:06,200 --> 00:28:08,828
So, I ascended that mountain twice or thrice that night.

383
00:28:09,725 --> 00:28:11,240
At last we reached Madina.

384
00:28:12,225 --> 00:28:16,789
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ sent his camels with his slave Rabah(رباح), and I was with him.

385
00:28:17,319 --> 00:28:22,128
I also went to the pasture with the horse of Talha(طلحة), along with his camels.

386
00:28:22,573 --> 00:28:29,420
See Salmah Ibn Akwah(سلمة إبن أكوع) was helping out Talha(طلحة) he was like a servant for him,

387
00:28:29,484 --> 00:28:31,911
so he would take his horse out to the pasture and take care of it.

388
00:28:32,966 --> 00:28:36,731
So he happened to be next to the shepherd of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

389
00:28:37,165 --> 00:28:41,481
When the day dawned Abdul Rahman Al-Fazari(عبدالرحمن ألفظاري) made a raid

390
00:28:41,576 --> 00:28:44,271
and drove away out of the camels of the Messenger of Allah,

391
00:28:44,795 --> 00:28:46,529
and killed the man who looked after them.

392
00:28:47,379 --> 00:28:54,555
So this is a man, who came with some Bedouins from Najd(نجد) and they raided the area surrounding Madina

393
00:28:54,595 --> 00:28:58,475
and they stole away the camels of Rasool Allah ﷺ and killed his shepherd.

394
00:28:59,491 --> 00:29:09,206
I said: Rabah(رباح) ride this horse, take it to Talha Bin Obaidillah(طلحة بن عبيدالله) and informed the Messenger of Allah,

395
00:29:09,682 --> 00:29:13,230
that the polytheists, have made away with his camels.

396
00:29:14,404 --> 00:29:15,865
Then I stood up on a hillock.

397
00:29:16,571 --> 00:29:20,085
I said: Rabah(رباح) ride this horse, take it to the Talha Bin Obaidillah(طلحة بن عبيدالله)

398
00:29:20,751 --> 00:29:25,644
and informed the Messenger of Allah, that the polytheists have made away with his camels.

399
00:29:26,585 --> 00:29:27,866
Then I stood upon a hillock

400
00:29:28,770 --> 00:29:32,889
and turning my face to Madina shouted thrice, come to our help.

401
00:29:33,739 --> 00:29:38,934
Then I set out in pursuit of the Raiders shooting at them with arrows and chanting poetry.

402
00:29:39,263 --> 00:29:43,052
I am the son of  Al-Akwah(ألأكوع), and today is the day of defeat for the mean.

403
00:29:44,168 --> 00:29:45,890
خُذْهَا وَاَنَا اِبْنِ الْاَكْوَعْ                       وَالْيَوْم يَوْمُ الرُّضَّعْ

404
00:29:47,548 --> 00:29:52,610
I would overtake a man from them shoot at him an arrow that would reach his shoulder.

405
00:29:53,356 --> 00:29:57,443
And I would say take it, and he would recite the same verses,

406
00:29:57,824 --> 00:29:59,618
خُذْهَا وَاَنَا اِبْنِ الْاَكْوَعْ                       وَالْيَوْم يَوْمُ الرُّضَّعْ

407
00:29:59,658 --> 00:30:01,347
So this was the slogan for the entire day.

408
00:30:02,577 --> 00:30:06,282
By God! I continued shooting at them and hamstringing their animals.

409
00:30:06,917 --> 00:30:12,918
Whenever a horseman turned upon me, I was coming to a tree and hid myself sitting at its base,

410
00:30:13,361 --> 00:30:16,492
then I would shoot at him and hamstrung his horse.

411
00:30:17,548 --> 00:30:19,976
At last they entered the narrow mountain gourds.

412
00:30:20,548 --> 00:30:24,980
I ascended that mountain and held them at bay by throwing stones at them.

413
00:30:26,046 --> 00:30:31,324
I continue to chase them in this way, until I got all the camels of the Messenger of Allah, released,

414
00:30:31,919 --> 00:30:33,395
and no camel was left with them.

415
00:30:34,689 --> 00:30:35,435
The left me.

416
00:30:36,475 --> 00:30:41,102
So they left him, but I followed them shooting at them continually

417
00:30:41,808 --> 00:30:46,761
until they dropped more than 30 mantle's on 30 Lance's, lighting their burden.

418
00:30:48,007 --> 00:30:51,851
On everything they dropped I put a mark with the help of a piece of stone.

419
00:30:52,343 --> 00:30:55,358
So Rasool Allah ﷺ and his companions might recognize them.

420
00:30:55,493 --> 00:31:01,897
So he's running, whenever they drop something he would leave mark over it and continue running .

421
00:31:02,222 --> 00:31:04,992
Salmah Ibn Akwah(سلمة إبن أكوع) was the fastest runner among the Sahabah(صحابه),

422
00:31:05,881 --> 00:31:11,383
Allah Alam(ألله اعلم), if this is an exaggeration, but they say that he would race with animals, camels horses.

423
00:31:12,699 --> 00:31:13,524
He was that fast.

424
00:31:16,016 --> 00:31:18,498
They went on until they came to a narrow valley.

425
00:31:18,879 --> 00:31:21,745
When so and so son of Badr Al-Fazari(بدرألفظاري) he joined them.

426
00:31:22,252 --> 00:31:27,205
They now sat down to take their breakfast, and I sat on top of a tapering rock.

427
00:31:28,213 --> 00:31:30,578
Al-Fazari(ألفظاري) said: Who is that fellow I'm seeing.

428
00:31:31,300 --> 00:31:33,228
They said: This fellow has harassed us.

429
00:31:33,852 --> 00:31:39,463
By Allah, He has not left us As dusk and has been continually shooting at us,

430
00:31:40,010 --> 00:31:42,536
until he smashed everything from our hands.

431
00:31:45,663 --> 00:31:48,576
He said: Four of you should make a dash at him, and kill him.

432
00:31:49,924 --> 00:31:54,034
Accordingly, four of them ascended the mountain, coming towards me,

433
00:31:54,327 --> 00:31:56,255
when it became possible for me to talk to them.

434
00:31:56,303 --> 00:31:57,557
I said: Do you recognize me.?

435
00:31:57,907 --> 00:31:58,899
They said: No! Who are you?

436
00:31:59,264 --> 00:32:00,920
I said: I am Salma son of Al-Akwah(أكوع).

437
00:32:01,777 --> 00:32:08,451
By the being, Who has honored the countenance of Muhammadﷺ I can kill any of you I like,

438
00:32:08,920 --> 00:32:10,551
but none of you will be able to kill me.

439
00:32:11,551 --> 00:32:13,348
One of them said: I think he's right!

440
00:32:21,392 --> 00:32:22,150
So they returned.

441
00:32:23,007 --> 00:32:29,487
I did not move from my place until I saw the Horsemen of Rasool Allah ﷺ came riding through the trees.

442
00:32:30,257 --> 00:32:34,562
Low the foremost among them was Akhram Al-Asdi(أخرم ألأسدي).

443
00:32:35,209 --> 00:32:39,915
Behind him was Abu Qatadah Al-Ansari(أبوقتادة ألأنصاري), and behind him was Al-Miqdad Al-Aswad Al-Kindi(ألمقداد بن ألأسود ألكندي).

444
00:32:40,284 --> 00:32:43,163
I can't hold up the reign of Akhram(أخرم)'s horse seeing this,

445
00:32:43,784 --> 00:32:44,958
they the Raiders fled.

446
00:32:45,149 --> 00:32:48,211
I said, to Akhram(أخرم), Akhram(أخرم) guard yourself against them,

447
00:32:48,513 --> 00:32:51,060
until Allah His Messenger and His companions join you.

448
00:32:51,663 --> 00:32:55,544
He said Salamah(سلمة), if you believe in Allah and the day of judgment.

449
00:32:56,115 --> 00:32:59,555
And if you know that paradise is reality and hell is reality.

450
00:32:59,976 --> 00:33:01,936
You should not stand between me and martyrdom.

451
00:33:03,262 --> 00:33:07,035
So I let him go Akhram(أخرم) and Abdur Rahman Al-Fazari(عبدالرحمن ألفظاري) met in combat,

452
00:33:07,868 --> 00:33:13,895
Akhram(أخرم) hamstrung Abdur-Rahman(عبدالرحمن)'s horse, and the ladder struck him with his lance and killed him.

453
00:33:13,950 --> 00:33:14,704
 So, Al-Akhram(أخرم) was killed.

454
00:33:15,554 --> 00:33:18,096
Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) turned about driving Akhram(أخرم)'s horse,

455
00:33:18,538 --> 00:33:21,257
Abu Qatadah(أبوقتادة), a horseman of the Messenger of Allah,

456
00:33:21,808 --> 00:33:25,348
met Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) in combat smote him with his lance and killed him.

457
00:33:26,276 --> 00:33:31,435
By the being who honored the countenance of Muhammadﷺ, I followed them running on my feet,

458
00:33:32,205 --> 00:33:38,967
so fast that I couldn't see behind me the companions of Muhammadﷺ, nor any dust raised by their horses.

459
00:33:40,467 --> 00:33:45,942
So he is running on foot, Faster than the horses behind them of Rasool Allah ﷺ and the Companions,

460
00:33:46,387 --> 00:33:47,860
he said: I couldn't even see them behind me.

461
00:33:49,161 --> 00:33:53,352
I followed them, until before sunset so this is an entire day.

462
00:33:53,550 --> 00:33:57,367
I mean from Fajr(فجر)  until sunset.

463
00:33:59,977 --> 00:34:04,242
So I followed them until before sunset they reached the Valley,

464
00:34:04,589 --> 00:34:07,642
which had the spring of water, which was called Zuqarad(ذوقرد)

465
00:34:08,062 --> 00:34:10,268
so that they could have a drink, for they were thirsty.

466
00:34:11,657 --> 00:34:13,106
They saw me running towards them.

467
00:34:14,142 --> 00:34:18,275
I turned them out of the valley before they could drink a drop of water,

468
00:34:18,634 --> 00:34:20,747
they left the valley and ran down the slope.

469
00:34:21,079 --> 00:34:28,393
I ran behind them over took a man from them, shot him with an arrow through the shoulder blade, and said:

470
00:34:28,472 --> 00:34:31,000
Take this, I'm the son of Al-Akwah(أكوع).

471
00:34:31,531 --> 00:34:34,349
And today is the day of annulations for the people who are mean,

472
00:34:34,850 --> 00:34:37,841
the fellow who was wounded said: May his mother weep over him,

473
00:34:37,881 --> 00:34:40,899
Are you the Akwah(أكوع), who has been chasing us since this morning.

474
00:34:41,494 --> 00:34:43,122
Are you the same Akwah(أكوع).?

475
00:34:44,384 --> 00:34:48,311
This guy he is injured, he's dying but he has that question of mind.

476
00:34:48,456 --> 00:34:51,045
He said: Is this the same Akwah(أكوع).?

477
00:34:51,736 --> 00:34:54,589
I said: Yes! O enemy of thyself, the same Akwah(أكوع).

478
00:34:55,453 --> 00:34:57,346
They'll have two horses dead tired,

479
00:34:57,386 --> 00:35:00,143
I mean the horses are dead tired, he's still running.

480
00:35:01,818 --> 00:35:04,555
The left two horses dead tired on the hillock.

481
00:35:05,198 --> 00:35:07,931
And I came dragging them along to the Messenger of Allah.

482
00:35:08,825 --> 00:35:14,010
I met Amir(عامر), who had with him a container, having milk diluted with water

483
00:35:14,228 --> 00:35:15,426
and a container having water.

484
00:35:16,045 --> 00:35:18,609
I performed Wudhoo(وضؤ) with the water and drank the milk.

485
00:35:19,458 --> 00:35:25,979
Then I came to Rasool Allah ﷺ while he was at the spring of water from which I had driven them away.

486
00:35:26,902 --> 00:35:29,899
Rasool Allah ﷺ had captured those camels and everything else,

487
00:35:29,994 --> 00:35:34,847
I had captured and all the Lancers and mantle's I had snatched from the Mushrikeen(مشركين)

488
00:35:35,490 --> 00:35:39,744
and Bilal(بلال) had slaughtered the she camel from the camels, I had seized from the people,

489
00:35:40,157 --> 00:35:43,070
and was roasting its liver and hump for the Messenger of Allah.

490
00:35:44,363 --> 00:35:49,314
I said: O Rasool Ullah. Let me select from our people 100 men,

491
00:35:49,760 --> 00:35:51,618
And I will follow the marauders,

492
00:35:52,216 --> 00:35:59,373
and I will finish them all, so that nobody is left to convey the news of their destruction to their people.

493
00:36:00,296 --> 00:36:03,209
At these words of mine. Rasool Allah ﷺ laughed, so much

494
00:36:04,017 --> 00:36:06,761
that his molar teeth could be seen in the light of the fire,

495
00:36:06,810 --> 00:36:08,583
he said: Salamah(سلمة), do you think you can do this.

496
00:36:08,972 --> 00:36:09,520
I said: Yes!

497
00:36:10,266 --> 00:36:11,858
By the being who has honored you.

498
00:36:12,782 --> 00:36:14,896
He said: Now they have reached the land of Ghatafan(غطافان)

499
00:36:15,317 --> 00:36:16,356
where they are being fed.

500
00:36:17,372 --> 00:36:19,975
At this time a man from Ghatafan(غطافان) came along and said:

501
00:36:20,253 --> 00:36:21,999
So and so slaughter the camel for them,

502
00:36:22,737 --> 00:36:24,844
when they were exposing it skin they saw dust.

503
00:36:25,479 --> 00:36:29,328
They said: They Akwah(أكوع) and his companions have come, so they went away fleeing.

504
00:36:31,249 --> 00:36:33,379
When it was morning the Messenger of Allah said:

505
00:36:33,459 --> 00:36:37,466
Our best horseman today is Abu Qatadah(أبوقتادة), and our best footman today is Salamah(سلمة).

506
00:36:38,545 --> 00:36:40,672
Then he gave me two shares of the booty.

507
00:36:41,228 --> 00:36:46,708
Share meant for the horsemen, and the share meant for the footmen, and combined both of them for me.

508
00:36:47,794 --> 00:36:49,572
This is in Muslim(ألمسلم) and Musnad Imam Ahmad(مَسند اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ).

509
00:36:50,636 --> 00:36:51,745
Now Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) says:

510
00:36:52,666 --> 00:36:59,222
In the request of Salamah(سلمة) to send with him 100 of the companions, is an evidence of the immense number of the enemy.

511
00:36:59,697 --> 00:37:01,527
Otherwise he wouldn't request such a number.

512
00:37:02,332 --> 00:37:07,794
So Salamah(سلمة) was pursuing an entire army on foot, alone, and he gave him such a hard time.

513
00:37:09,405 --> 00:37:11,802
This is another interesting story.

514
00:37:12,485 --> 00:37:16,516
Abul-Ala Bin Hazrami(أبوالأعلى بن حض) said: Bisr Bin Artaa(بسر بن أرطأة) attacked the land of the Romans.

515
00:37:16,961 --> 00:37:18,143
Do you remember Bisr Bin Artaa(بسر بن أرطأة)?

516
00:37:19,223 --> 00:37:25,897
He was the Ameer(أمير) of the army, when Abu Muslim Al-Khaulani(أبومسلم ألخولاني) went to him and asked him,

517
00:37:25,937 --> 00:37:27,590
to appoint him as the leader of the Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء).

518
00:37:28,280 --> 00:37:30,804
It was Bisr Bin Artaa(بسر بن أرطأة) who was the leader of that army.

519
00:37:32,193 --> 00:37:35,627
So but the rear of his army was constantly attacked

520
00:37:35,770 --> 00:37:40,306
and whenever he would prepare a trap for the attackers, his soldiers would be attacked instead.

521
00:37:41,766 --> 00:37:46,443
So he decided to stay behind with 100 of his soldiers to figure out who was ambushing them.

522
00:37:47,935 --> 00:37:54,723
One day he went alone in one of the valleys and found 30 horses, tied next to a monastery with the Knights inside it,

523
00:37:54,910 --> 00:37:58,855
 he realized that this was the group who were ambushing his army.

524
00:37:59,552 --> 00:38:01,609
So he tied his horse next to the monastery

525
00:38:02,211 --> 00:38:07,093
and went in and close the door behind him, preventing them from leaving.

526
00:38:08,030 --> 00:38:10,491
He then started fighting them single handedly.

527
00:38:11,109 --> 00:38:15,033
And by the time they were able to lay their hands on their weapons he had already killed three of them.

528
00:38:16,486 --> 00:38:20,360
When Bisr(بسر)'s Soldiers discovered his absence, they went searching for him

529
00:38:20,780 --> 00:38:22,972
and came by the monastery and found his horse.

530
00:38:23,264 --> 00:38:25,884
They also heard the noise coming from inside the monastery,

531
00:38:26,264 --> 00:38:30,029
so they tried getting in, but the door was closed.

532
00:38:30,873 --> 00:38:34,992
So they had to break off some panels from the roof and then descended into the monastery.

533
00:38:35,890 --> 00:38:39,464
They found him fighting the knights, with his sword in one hand

534
00:38:40,139 --> 00:38:43,871
and the other hand was holding some of his intestines that had spilled out.

535
00:38:44,950 --> 00:38:46,513
He then fell down unconscious.

536
00:38:47,252 --> 00:38:50,936
His soldiers continued the fight killing some and capturing the rest.

537
00:38:51,473 --> 00:38:53,283
The captured, ask the soldiers.

538
00:38:53,695 --> 00:38:56,581
We ask you in the name of God, who is that man.

539
00:38:57,620 --> 00:39:00,819
They said: He is Bisr Bin Artaa(بسر بن أرطأة), the Roman knights said:

540
00:39:01,223 --> 00:39:05,664
In the name of God, no woman has ever given birth to anyone like him.

541
00:39:06,814 --> 00:39:12,658
The soldiers then put the hanging intestines back into his stomach, since none of them was punctured.

542
00:39:13,624 --> 00:39:16,251
They tied his stomach with some of their turbans

543
00:39:16,830 --> 00:39:20,099
and they carried him back, then his stomach was stitched and he was cured.

544
00:39:24,519 --> 00:39:29,251
There's a difference of opinion on whether Bisr(بسر) was a companion or a Tabae(تابعي).

545
00:39:29,370 --> 00:39:32,738
He was one of the most courageous of this nation.

546
00:39:34,567 --> 00:39:36,162
Al-Bara Bin Aazib(ألبراءبن عازب) narrates,

547
00:39:38,709 --> 00:39:40,893
Allah's apostle sent Abdullah Bin Atiq(عبدالله بن عتيق)

548
00:39:42,949 --> 00:39:48,355
and Abdullah Bin Utbah(عبدالله بن عتبة) the group of men to Abu Rafia(أبورافع) to kill him.

549
00:39:50,316 --> 00:39:52,792
They proceeded till they approached his castles,

550
00:39:52,832 --> 00:39:57,682
so this was an assassination mission, appointed by Rasool Allah ﷺ.

551
00:39:57,746 --> 00:40:02,551
Rasool Allah ﷺ appointed Abdullah Bin Atiq(عبدالله بن عتيق) to assassinate, Abi Rafia(أبي رافع),

552
00:40:02,591 --> 00:40:10,752
Abi Rafia(أبي رافع) was a wealthy trader in Hijaz(حجاز), causing the Muslims, so much trouble.

553
00:40:11,577 --> 00:40:16,974
So Rasool Allah ﷺ sanctioned his assassination and he appointed Abdullah Bin Atiq(عبدالله بن عتيق)

554
00:40:17,679 --> 00:40:21,407
and some of the other Ansaar(أنصار) to this special operation.

555
00:40:22,971 --> 00:40:25,190
So they proceeded till they approached his castle

556
00:40:25,793 --> 00:40:28,817
where upon Abdullah Bin Atiq(عبدالله بن عتيق) said to them, wait here!

557
00:40:29,245 --> 00:40:31,138
And in the meantime I will go and see.

558
00:40:33,177 --> 00:40:38,098
Abdullah(عبدالله) said: Later on, I played a trick, in order to enter the castle.

559
00:40:38,852 --> 00:40:45,385
By chance they lost the donkey of theirs and came out carrying a flaming light to search for it.

560
00:40:45,930 --> 00:40:49,432
I was afraid that they would recognize me, so I covered my head and legs

561
00:40:49,750 --> 00:40:52,871
and pretended that I was answering the call to nature.

562
00:40:53,569 --> 00:40:56,522
So you know, this is castle, everybody is known in there.

563
00:40:57,887 --> 00:41:02,026
And these castles close at night, they close at night.

564
00:41:03,415 --> 00:41:08,015
So he covered his head, and sat down pretending that he's responding to the call of nature,

565
00:41:09,375 --> 00:41:14,891
so that when they come back they think that he is somebody from the castle who came out to respond, the call of nature,

566
00:41:14,931 --> 00:41:18,113
you don't have toilets in there, you have to go out.

567
00:41:20,232 --> 00:41:22,700
So, this is the trick he used.

568
00:41:22,938 --> 00:41:27,226
So the gatekeeper called, whoever wants to come in should come in before I close the gate.

569
00:41:27,773 --> 00:41:32,742
So I went in and hid myself in the stall of a donkey, near the gate of the castle.

570
00:41:33,758 --> 00:41:36,924
They took their supper with Abu Rafia(أبورافع) and had a chat till late night.

571
00:41:38,440 --> 00:41:41,758
Then they went back to their homes, when the voices vanished,

572
00:41:41,992 --> 00:41:44,548
and I no longer detected any movement I came out.

573
00:41:46,032 --> 00:41:51,002
I had seen where the gatekeeper had kept the key of the castle in a hole in the wall.

574
00:41:51,691 --> 00:41:59,236
So I took it and unlocked the gate of the castle, saying to myself, if these people should notice me I will run away easily.

575
00:42:00,244 --> 00:42:04,291
Then I locked all the doors of their houses from outside, while they're inside.

576
00:42:05,307 --> 00:42:06,555
So, he locked them up

577
00:42:08,023 --> 00:42:11,485
and ascended to Abu Rafia(أبورافع) via staircase.

578
00:42:12,118 --> 00:42:16,345
I saw the house in complete darkness with its lights, with its lights off.

579
00:42:16,385 --> 00:42:17,273
Now listen to this!

580
00:42:18,003 --> 00:42:18,797
So the lights are off.

581
00:42:19,908 --> 00:42:23,146
And he is inside the house of Abu Rafia(أبورافع), he wants to know, where Abu Rafia(أبورافع) is?

582
00:42:24,114 --> 00:42:26,032
and I could not know where the man was,

583
00:42:26,619 --> 00:42:28,026
so I called O Abu Rafia(أبورافع).!

584
00:42:31,262 --> 00:42:32,278
He replied, who is it?

585
00:42:33,103 --> 00:42:35,038
I proceeded towards the voice and hit him.

586
00:42:38,533 --> 00:42:41,122
He cried loudly, but my blow was futile.

587
00:42:42,262 --> 00:42:43,035
Then look at this,

588
00:42:43,115 --> 00:42:45,440
Then I came to him pretending to help him,

589
00:42:46,694 --> 00:42:48,250
saying with a different tone of voice,

590
00:42:48,639 --> 00:42:51,588
now he changed his voice as if he's the guard he is going to help him.

591
00:42:53,042 --> 00:42:54,494
What is wrong with you, Abu Rafia(أبورافع).

592
00:42:55,026 --> 00:43:00,702
He said: Are you not surprised, woe onto your mother, a man has come to me and hit me with a sword.

593
00:43:01,304 --> 00:43:03,011
So again I aimed at him and hit him.

594
00:43:05,804 --> 00:43:08,631
But the blow proved futile again.

595
00:43:09,306 --> 00:43:12,147
And on that Abu Rafia(أبورافع) cried loudly and his wife got up.

596
00:43:13,036 --> 00:43:16,859
I came again and change my voice as if I were a helper,

597
00:43:17,390 --> 00:43:20,233
and I found Abu Rafia(أبورافع) laying straight on his back.

598
00:43:21,017 --> 00:43:24,081
So I drove the sword into his belly and bent on it,

599
00:43:24,787 --> 00:43:27,208
till I heard the sound of his spine break.

600
00:43:28,009 --> 00:43:30,789
So he cracked the spine with the sword, that's it, it's certain death.

601
00:43:31,920 --> 00:43:36,076
Then I came out, filled with astonishment and went to the staircase to descend,

602
00:43:36,322 --> 00:43:39,547
but I fell down from it and got my leg, dislocated.

603
00:43:40,693 --> 00:43:44,082
I bandage it and went to my companions limping,

604
00:43:44,281 --> 00:43:47,446
I said to them: Go and tell Allah's Apostle of this good news,

605
00:43:47,762 --> 00:43:52,022
but I will not leave this place till I hear the news of his death.

606
00:43:53,070 --> 00:43:57,286
Now you know the pain of a dislocated foot, extremely painful.

607
00:43:58,641 --> 00:44:03,614
He wrapped it with his turban, and he refused to leave.

608
00:44:04,932 --> 00:44:10,422
He wanted to stay behind, so that he would actually hear the announcement that Abu Rafia(أبورافع) is dead.

609
00:44:10,469 --> 00:44:12,651
Now when you crack the spine of somebody, he is dead.

610
00:44:13,509 --> 00:44:18,677
But this shows you that the Sahabah(صحابه) took their missions, extremely seriously.

611
00:44:18,907 --> 00:44:22,118
This is Ibkan Ul-Amal(إتقان العمل), this is perfection of your work.

612
00:44:23,407 --> 00:44:30,409
He's gonna hang around to make sure that he has fulfilled the mission that was appointed to him by Rasool Allah ﷺ.

613
00:44:31,322 --> 00:44:35,920
It is tells you the difference between the true dedicated Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله)

614
00:44:36,182 --> 00:44:39,629
and the one, who's out there and acting in the movie.

615
00:44:40,650 --> 00:44:44,533
When dawn broke, an announcer of death got over the wall and announced,

616
00:44:45,120 --> 00:44:47,687
I convey to you the news of Abu Rafia(أبورافع)'s as death.

617
00:44:48,414 --> 00:44:50,748
I got up and proceeded without feeling any pain,

618
00:44:51,319 --> 00:44:56,584
until I  caught up with my companions before they reach the Prophet to whom I conveyed the good news to.

619
00:44:56,972 --> 00:45:00,448
In another narration it says that he actually did go and he had a lot of pain,

620
00:45:00,995 --> 00:45:05,397
Rasool Allah ﷺ, placed his hand over his foot and he immediately cured.

621
00:45:06,501 --> 00:45:09,646
Now this Hadith(حديث) is quoted in the section here.

622
00:45:10,667 --> 00:45:16,397
But I think that this lesson that I mentioned, it is extremely important point that that needs to be highlighted

623
00:45:17,128 --> 00:45:21,210
that, you know, perfection in such work is extremely important.

624
00:45:22,814 --> 00:45:24,159
Perfection, patience.

625
00:45:24,802 --> 00:45:30,314
There is an army magazine in America called the American GI,

626
00:45:30,857 --> 00:45:34,668
they wrote an article about the Mujahideen(مجاهدين) in the Philippines.

627
00:45:36,287 --> 00:45:37,391
This was a few years ago,

628
00:45:38,256 --> 00:45:48,505
they said that some of these soldiers are so dedicated, you could post them on monitoring position on top of the tree,

629
00:45:49,918 --> 00:45:56,308
 they would be in camouflage, and they would wait there for days without moving.

630
00:45:57,869 --> 00:46:01,582
So this is Sabr(صبر), I mean this is Ribat(رباط) staying there for days and not moving.

631
00:46:02,304 --> 00:46:06,551
And the battle of Al-Qadsiya(ألقادسية), the Muslims were a little over 7000.

632
00:46:07,646 --> 00:46:12,796
While the non believers were 40 or 70,000 accompanied by 70 elephants.

633
00:46:13,980 --> 00:46:16,075
Al-Tartushi(ألطرطوشي) mentions in Siraj Ul-Malook(سراج الملوك),

634
00:46:16,869 --> 00:46:21,512
that Amr Bin Madiyakrib(عمروبن معديكرب) went next to the river and told his people.

635
00:46:22,178 --> 00:46:28,177
I'm going to cross the bridge, if you follow me after a time equivalent to the time it takes to slaughter a camel.

636
00:46:28,653 --> 00:46:34,674
You will find me with a sword in my hand fighting whoever is in front of me, and the enemies surrounding me.

637
00:46:35,056 --> 00:46:36,199
And I'm standing between them.

638
00:46:36,945 --> 00:46:39,518
If you come later than that, you would find me dead.

639
00:46:41,231 --> 00:46:44,059
And then he crossed the bridge over the river towards the enemy's camp.

640
00:46:44,305 --> 00:46:46,493
A while later, his people said: O sons of the Zabeed(زبيد)!

641
00:46:47,027 --> 00:46:50,617
Are we going to leave our man alone, we might not even catch him alive.

642
00:46:51,504 --> 00:46:54,696
So they crossed the bridge, and found him without his horse.

643
00:46:55,601 --> 00:47:01,602
While he was holding both back legs of an enemy's horse and the horse failed to move,

644
00:47:02,843 --> 00:47:06,854
the fighter on the horse was trying to reach Amr(عمرو) behind him with his sword with no avail.

645
00:47:07,573 --> 00:47:10,943
When the fighter saw us attacking he came down from his horse and ran away.

646
00:47:11,687 --> 00:47:15,973
Amr(عمرو) then mounted the horse. He then told us you were almost going to miss me.

647
00:47:16,846 --> 00:47:20,150
They asked him: Where's your horse he said it was hit by an arrow that killed it.

648
00:47:20,752 --> 00:47:22,363
And I fell off its back.

649
00:47:24,872 --> 00:47:26,934
And imagine a man holding a horse.

650
00:47:27,649 --> 00:47:30,794
Al-Tartushi(ألطرطوشي) mentions in Siraj Ul-Malook(سراج الملوك) and Al-Qurtubi(ألقرطبي) in his history

651
00:47:30,881 --> 00:47:36,613
that Tariq bin Ziad(طارق بن زياد), crossing into Andalusia, Spain, with 1700 Men.

652
00:47:37,554 --> 00:47:41,411
Tazfir(تضفر) was the deputy of Ruzreeq(رزريق), Ruzreeq(رزريق), is Rodriguez.

653
00:47:42,086 --> 00:47:46,183
And he fought with Tariq(طارق) and his army for three continuous days.

654
00:47:46,798 --> 00:47:50,117
He sent a message to Ruzreeq(رزريق), that some people crossed over to us.

655
00:47:50,584 --> 00:47:54,023
And I don't know whether they belong to this earth, or they came from the heaven.

656
00:47:54,857 --> 00:47:56,925
We have no capability of fighting them alone.

657
00:47:57,305 --> 00:48:00,305
So we urge you to come and assist us yourself.

658
00:48:01,439 --> 00:48:04,134
Tazfir(تضفر) came with an enforcement of 90,000 strong.

659
00:48:04,745 --> 00:48:06,673
They fought with the Muslims for another three days,

660
00:48:07,515 --> 00:48:09,951
things we're tightening on the Muslims so Tariq(طارق) told them:

661
00:48:10,689 --> 00:48:12,689
You have no refuge but in your swords.

662
00:48:13,411 --> 00:48:14,377
Where are you going to go.?

663
00:48:15,520 --> 00:48:18,725
When you are in the middle of your enemy's territory and the seas behind you.

664
00:48:19,503 --> 00:48:22,360
I'm going to do something that would bring either Victory or death,

665
00:48:22,543 --> 00:48:23,653
they said what are you going to do.?

666
00:48:24,260 --> 00:48:26,210
He said: I will attack their leader straight on.

667
00:48:26,879 --> 00:48:28,704
If you see me charged than charge with me.

668
00:48:29,344 --> 00:48:33,940
They did that Ruzreeq(رزريق) was killed, along with many of his soldiers and they were defeated.

669
00:48:34,438 --> 00:48:36,531
Only a small number of Muslims were killed.

670
00:48:36,930 --> 00:48:39,922
Tariq(طارق) then sent the head of Ruzreeq(رزريق) to Musa Bin Nusair(موسى بن نصير) in Africa.

671
00:48:41,096 --> 00:48:44,738
And Musa(موسى) sent it to the Khalifah(خليفه), Al-Walid Bin Abdul Malik(ألوليد بن عبدالملك) in Damascus.

672
00:48:46,071 --> 00:48:53,039
Sabith(ثابت) narrated that Ikrimah(عكرمة), the son of Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) dismounted his horse in battle,

673
00:48:53,918 --> 00:48:57,703
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) told him: Don't do that, your death would be hard on the Muslims,

674
00:48:57,838 --> 00:48:59,679
he replied Oh Khalid(خالد) leave me alone!

675
00:49:00,473 --> 00:49:07,243
You became a Muslim with the Messenger of Allah, while my father and myself were the worst and animosity against him.

676
00:49:08,028 --> 00:49:09,685
He fought on foot until he was killed.

677
00:49:11,098 --> 00:49:12,823
He died in the battle of Yarmook(يرموك).

678
00:49:13,844 --> 00:49:18,226
Malik Ibn Dinar(مالك إبن دينار) said: During the Battle of Zawiya(زاوية) Abdullah Bin Gharif(عبدالله بن غارف) said:

679
00:49:18,306 --> 00:49:22,932
I am seeing something I cannot hold back from, let's head to paradise.

680
00:49:23,631 --> 00:49:26,608
He then broke the sheath of his sword and fought until he was killed.

681
00:49:27,076 --> 00:49:30,427
When he was buried his grave would give off the smell of musk.

682
00:49:31,211 --> 00:49:36,978
I went myself to his grave and picked up some of his dirt and smelled Musk emanating from it.

683
00:49:37,372 --> 00:49:42,987
This is by the way, one of the most predominant Karamat(کرامات) of the Mujahideen(مجاهدين), in our current age.

